    "updated_at": "2026-11-02T22:36:15Z",
    "body": "Yes please to this feature! We've mainted a `disabledFocusable` prop on all button and button-like components largely for this reason (i.e. there are multiple scenarios when a button or menuitem can become disabled on activation). It requires using `aria-disabled`, `tabindex`, and javascript event handling to do, and is a pain. Having this and being able to retire that code would be lovely.\n\n@zcorpan I can't think of any immediate backwards compat issues right now. Any focus management scripting should still work, and a user's focus not getting bounced shouldn't change much for authors, I think 🤞.\n\nI am assuming calling `element.focus()` still wouldn't work, but please correct me if I'm wrong about that. That'd be a bigger authoring difference if it did.",
