    "body": "> I am assuming calling `element.focus()` still wouldn't work, but please correct me if I'm wrong about that. That'd be a bigger authoring difference if it did.\n\nRight. Literally this would be new code paths to avoid the focus bounce (and subsequently prevent stuff like keypress, close open pickers, etc), but the existing code paths like moving focus onto disabled elements, tabindex, calling `.focus()` would do the old behaviour (which is to say: there'd be no way to get an element in focus, if it is disabled, other than being already on it when it transitions).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
