    "created_at": "2026-11-04T15:48:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-05T21:56:42Z",
    "body": "I checked compat with a Firefox build of bug 2087206 against Common Crawl and HTTP Archive. It looks compatible, with one rare and mild case: a second Enter on a focused disabled control can repeat a page's action.\n\nAI summary of the research ([zcorpan/disabled-focus-compat](https://github.com/zcorpan/disabled-focus-compat)):\n\n> Common Crawl (255,716 pages, inline scripts) and the HTTP Archive 10k sample (root pages, external scripts too) were searched for script that disables something near Enter handling, blur/focusout or `activeElement`. Matches were grouped and reviewed. Testable hits were loaded in Firefox with `dom.forms.retain_focus_on_disabled.enabled` off and on, and with a variant that sends key events to the body while the focused control is disabled.\n>\n> | | Common Crawl | HTTP Archive (desktop / mobile) |\n> |---|---|---|\n> | Enter handler disables its own control, no guard | 22 pages (0.0086%) | 2 / 2 of 5,991 / 7,203 |\n> | Depends on blur/focusout or `activeElement` after disabling | 0 of 55 groups | |\n>\n> Live, 3 of 3 testable pages repeated the action with the change, and none did with the variant:\n> - prosol-farben.de: a second search request\n> - kamo.com: the same navigation restarted\n> - masutabe.info (nsfw): the same navigation restarted\n>\n> The crawl also has 4 pages where the repeat would be a POST (a chat, a newsletter signup, comments). Sending key events to the body while the focused control is disabled avoids the repeats and keeps focus. Several focus traps and refocus helpers improve.\n>\n> The repeat comes from the PR's key event steps, not the Gecko patch: they still fire key events at the focused disabled control, so its listeners run. Blocking the events instead would also drop document-level key handling and the later blur/change ([why](https://github.com/zcorpan/disabled-focus-compat/blob/main/README.md#1-why-a-second-enter-repeats-the-pages-action)).\n>\n> Details: [README](https://github.com/zcorpan/disabled-focus-compat/blob/main/README.md)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
